 md.push_str("\nDIRECT and TLS use the exact same executable and arithmetic functions; the A negative-control labels invoke the same API. The new driver selects `D` for direct B and `B` for TLS B; original controls retain the byte-exact original driver. Consequently comparisons with original artifacts also contain a driver/call-layout difference. Same-artifact equivalence does not establish universal absence of TLS or layout effects.\n\nThe preregistered explanatory condition fails; the ±2% condition passes. The primary32 DIRECT/TLS median is 0.996412 [0.982218, 1.008455]; grouped2x232 is 1.001685 [0.992440, 1.014943]. Bounds are ranks4..12/15, nominal96.484375% marginal median coverage conditional on exchangeable blocks, not familywise. No observation is excluded, extended or rerun. Known fresh/FROZEN primary32 is0.926947 [0.914657,0.937000], and grouped2x232 is0.908046 [0.898062,0.915495]. The persistent gap is not an accepted SDK gain and remains unexplained.\n\nThe immutable native design had a reversed explanatory ratio direction and an insufficient upper-bound requirement. Before any recording, the separately pinned protocol corrects this to TLS/DIRECT upper<1 with at least10/15wins, plus DIRECT/known-fresh lower>1 and median>=1.03 in bothB32. All sample counts, cases and diagnostics stay fixed. Native source/results do not change; no successful qualification or measurement is repeated for the clarification.\n\n## CPU, memory and profiles\n\nSeparate warm PMU panels give the following primary32 values per query. All four events have qualified running coverage; these single panels are diagnostics, not confidence intervals or causal decomposition.\n\n|Arm|Instructions M|User cycles M|Generic cache misses M|\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n");
